{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Sarek_metal.Metal_api</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"sarek-metal","href":"../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Sarek_metal","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Metal_api","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[{"title":"Exceptions","href":"#exceptions","children":[]},{"title":"Device Management","href":"#device-management","children":[]},{"title":"Host memory","href":"#host-memory","children":[]},{"title":"Command Queue Management","href":"#command-queue-management","children":[]},{"title":"Memory Management","href":"#memory-management","children":[]},{"title":"Library and Function Management","href":"#library-and-function-management","children":[]},{"title":"Compute Pipeline Management","href":"#compute-pipeline-management","children":[]},{"title":"Kernel Execution","href":"#kernel-execution","children":[]},{"title":"Synchronization","href":"#synchronization","children":[]},{"title":"Profiling","href":"#profiling","children":[]}],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-memcpy_lazy\"><a href=\"#val-memcpy_lazy\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> memcpy_lazy : \u000A  <span><span>(<span><span>unit <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Ctypes_static</span>.ptr</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A    <span><span>unit <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Ctypes_static</span>.ptr</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A    <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Unsigned</span>.size_t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A    <span>unit <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Ctypes_static</span>.ptr</span>)</span>\u000A    lazy_t</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>memcpy from libc for memory transfers, with the OCaml runtime lock released (a large copy would otherwise stop every other domain's minor collections). Both arguments are raw addresses, which the call does not root: the caller keeps the memory behind them allocated until <code>memcpy</code> returns (bigarrays end with <code>ignore (Sys.opaque_identity ba)</code>; MTLBuffer <code>contents</code> stays valid while the buffer is retained). See <a href=\"../Metal_bindings/index.html#val-msg_void_blocking_lazy\"><code>Metal_bindings.msg_void_blocking_lazy</code></a>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-memcpy\"><a href=\"#val-memcpy\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> memcpy : \u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">dst</span>:<span>unit <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Ctypes_static</span>.ptr</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">src</span>:<span>unit <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Ctypes_static</span>.ptr</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">size</span>:int <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  unit</span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"exceptions\"><a href=\"#exceptions\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Exceptions</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec exception anchored\" id=\"exception-Metal_error\"><a href=\"#exception-Metal_error\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">exception</span> </span><span><span class=\"exception\">Metal_error</span> <span class=\"keyword\">of</span> string</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Deprecated: no longer raised. <code>check</code> below now raises the canonical <a href=\"../Metal_error/index.html#exception-Metal_error\"><code>Metal_error.Metal_error</code></a> (a <code>Backend_error</code> alias) via the shared <a href=\"../../../spoc/Sarek_backend_error/Backend_error/Make/index.html#val-check\"><code>Sarek_backend_error.Backend_error.Make.check</code></a> funnel. Kept only so out-of-tree code matching on <code>Metal_api.Metal_error msg</code> still compiles (this library is opam-published).</p><ul class=\"at-tags\"><li class=\"deprecated\"><span class=\"at-tag\">deprecated</span> no longer raised; Metal_api.check now raises Metal_error.Metal_error (Backend_error) - catch that instead</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-check\"><a href=\"#val-check\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> check : <span>string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"../Metal_types/index.html#type-mtl_error\">Metal_types.mtl_error</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Check Metal result and raise a canonical <code>Backend_error</code> on failure.</p></div></div><h2 id=\"device-management\"><a href=\"#device-management\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Device Management</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Device\"><a href=\"#module-Device\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Device/index.html\">Device</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"host-memory\"><a href=\"#host-memory\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Host memory</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-page_size\"><a href=\"#val-page_size\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> page_size : <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> int</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The OS page size in bytes (16384 on Apple silicon).</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-alloc_aligned\"><a href=\"#val-alloc_aligned\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> alloc_aligned : <span><span class=\"label\">byte_size</span>:int <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> nativeint</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>byte_size</code> bytes of host memory aligned to the OS page size (<code>posix_memalign</code>), uninitialised. Released only by <a href=\"#val-free_aligned\"><code>free_aligned</code></a>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-free_aligned\"><a href=\"#val-free_aligned\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> free_aligned : <span>nativeint <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"command-queue-management\"><a href=\"#command-queue-management\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Command Queue Management</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-CommandQueue\"><a href=\"#module-CommandQueue\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"CommandQueue/index.html\">CommandQueue</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-mark_fast_math_fallback\"><a href=\"#val-mark_fast_math_fallback\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> mark_fast_math_fallback : <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Without the conformant compile options the device compiler runs in Metal's fast-math mode, which may reassociate: a fused epilogue kernel is then no longer guaranteed to equal the unfused pair. Mark Metal inexact so epilogue fusion stays off (docs/fp-contraction-policy.md section 14, <a href=\"../../../sarek/Spoc_framework_registry/Fp_exactness/index.html\"><code>Spoc_framework_registry.Fp_exactness</code></a>).</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-probe_conformant_options\"><a href=\"#val-probe_conformant_options\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> probe_conformant_options : <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Build the conformant options once at start-up, so a fallback is known before the first launch decides whether to fuse an epilogue.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-force_all\"><a href=\"#val-force_all\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> force_all : <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Force every lazily built FFI stub on the launch, copy and release paths (see <a href=\"../Metal_bindings/index.html#val-force_all\"><code>Metal_bindings.force_all</code></a>).</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Pending\"><a href=\"#module-Pending\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Pending/index.html\">Pending</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"memory-management\"><a href=\"#memory-management\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Memory Management</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Memory\"><a href=\"#module-Memory\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Memory/index.html\">Memory</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"library-and-function-management\"><a href=\"#library-and-function-management\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Library and Function Management</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Library\"><a href=\"#module-Library\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Library/index.html\">Library</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"compute-pipeline-management\"><a href=\"#compute-pipeline-management\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Compute Pipeline Management</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-ComputePipeline\"><a href=\"#module-ComputePipeline\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"ComputePipeline/index.html\">ComputePipeline</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"kernel-execution\"><a href=\"#kernel-execution\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Kernel Execution</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Kernel\"><a href=\"#module-Kernel\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Kernel/index.html\">Kernel</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"synchronization\"><a href=\"#synchronization\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Synchronization</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-synchronize\"><a href=\"#val-synchronize\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> synchronize : <span><span class=\"type-var\">'a</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div></div><h2 id=\"profiling\"><a href=\"#profiling\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Profiling</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Profiling\"><a href=\"#module-Profiling\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Profiling/index.html\">Profiling</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div>"}